{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1155233-donna-brazill-comes-clean-on-dnc-corruption","id":1155233,"title":"Donna Brazill comes clean on DNC corruption","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-02T17:55:36-07:00","id":1155233,"title":"Donna Brazill comes clean on DNC corruption","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TkoIWg0p_f0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TkoIWg0p_f0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/TkoIWg0p_f0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/TkoIWg0p_f0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It's worse then I imagined, the DNC was basically owned by the Hillary camp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T18:43:53-07:00","id":1155245,"title":"","content":"I dunno, forums user Omegaphallic. Isn't Donna a woman? You have to be really careful about trusting women.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-02T19:38:41-07:00","id":1155258,"title":"","content":"Donna Brazile is the same person who admitted to feeding the Clinton campaign debate questions. I don't know why she's throwing shade at Hillary now, but I would take her claims with a grain of salt until they're verified by a nonpartisan third party.<br /> <br /> Normally I don't like to assume malice, but the first explanation I can think of for her behavior is &quot;She's trying to get in good with the progressive wing of the Democratic party - it's her best shot at another campaign job after the 2016 campaign controversies. That, or profit from them.&quot; Certainly, I don't see the use in making accusations of people who aren't in power anymore.<br /> <br /> EDIT: For clarification, I haven't read her book, only the Politico article she wrote. I generally distrust chronicles that are written like thrillers, and this is no exception.<br /> <a href=\"https://www.politico.com/magazine/story/2017/11/02/clinton-brazile-hacks-2016-215774?lo=ap_e1\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.politico.com/magazine/st...15774?lo=ap_e1</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":". 11-02-2017, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T01:55:24-07:00","id":1155328,"title":"","content":"Because yelling about HRC means anything in 2017....<br /> <br /> Also Donna Brazile's story is entirely to self serving. Important facts she leaves out:<br /> <br /> 1) The joint fundraising agreements had been DNC procedure for multiple cycles before this. They've been a long standing method of getting money for the party (whether you like that or not is largely irrelevant to this, and Tom Perez and Keith Ellison already revised these things before this came out).<br /> <br /> 2) The agreements raised money for the DNC regardless of who was nominated, because the whole point is that it creates a larger war chest for the general and down ballot races. That's why in contested primaries, both candidates do it However:<br /> <br /> 3) Sanders signed up for the same joint fundraising agreements that Clinton did (in 2015, as was publicly reported), and then didn't use them. So... the Clinton campaign's ability to control the DNC is because Sanders didn't play ball (and it's not like he wasn't doing well fundraising-wise). If Sanders had participated (like Clinton did when she lost to Obama), there wouldn't have been the opening for Clinton to have so much influence, and there would have been better support for down ballot races (which considering how damned close the Senate and House have been on key votes, could have been really damned useful! However bad the math looks for Clinton according to Brazile it's still more than Sanders did by going outside the DNC systems).<br /> <br /> 4) Donna Brazile was a DNC officer the whole time. Her story makes it sound like her interim appointment to chair the DNC meant she came in not knowing about any of this. <b>She was the vice-chair</b> before that. If she didn't know about any of this until her appointment as interim chair, she didn't want to know. This is the biggest reason to be highly critical of her motives in writing this. It paints her own role as innocent, however it could not have gotten that bad without her complicit involvement, or negligence to her duties as a DNC officer. If you take her at her face, she spent months accepting, &quot;everything's fine!&quot; without any numbers, details, reports, or whatnot, and... somehow that's not her fault.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T15:49:00-07:00","id":1155568,"title":"","content":"Honestly it's a huge mess, the DNC is in need of radical reform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T17:03:11-07:00","id":1155585,"title":"","content":"Is it? It certainly needs to change and adapt, and that's happening already.<br /> <br /> Radical change seems pointless if it just means being worse at getting liberals and progressives elected, or going down the RNC's ideological rabbit hole where they've chained themselves to sinking ever farther down performative purity over actual policy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T06:45:02-07:00","id":1155717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1155233-donna-brazill-comes-clean-on-dnc-corruption?p=1155328#post1155328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because yelling about HRC means anything in 2017....<br /> <br /> Also Donna Brazile's story is entirely to self serving. Important facts she leaves out:<br /> <br /> 1) The joint fundraising agreements had been DNC procedure for multiple cycles before this. They've been a long standing method of getting money for the party (whether you like that or not is largely irrelevant to this, and Tom Perez and Keith Ellison already revised these things before this came out).</div> </div> </div> </div>I am under the impression that Donna's story is <i>not</i> about joint fundraising agreements, but rather is about a completely separate and highly questionable agreement that the DNC signed with Clinton which gave Clinton an unusual amount of control over the DNC.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"http://www.cnn.com/2017/11/03/politics/dnc-clinton-memorandum-of-understanding/index.html\" target=\"_blank\">(CNN)</a> - Hillary Clinton's campaign and the Democratic National Committee signed a memorandum of understanding in August 2015 that stated in return for their financial support, the campaign would require &quot;appropriate influence over the financial, strategic and operational use of these (Joint Fundraising Agreement) raised funds&quot; for general election expenditures, according to a copy of the agreement obtained by CNN.<br /> <br /> The agreement established rules and guidance around the separate joint fundraising agreement Clinton's campaign signed with the DNC. It was sent to Amy Dacey, the then-CEO of the DNC, from Robby Mook, Clinton's campaign manager, on August 26, 2015.<br /> <br /> The document provides context to a bombshell book excerpt published earlier this week by interim DNC chair Donna Brazile, which alleges that an unethical agreement was signed between Clinton's 2016 presidential campaign and the DNC to keep the party financially afloat. The memorandum of understanding appears to match the document described by Brazile.<br /> <br /> According to a copy obtained by CNN, the document does not give the Clinton campaign outright authority to make staffing decisions for the DNC, but it does give the Clinton campaign a say in who the DNC considers for positions like communications director and senior staff in communications and technology and research departments.<br /> <br /> <b>Initially, Democrats believed that Brazile was referencing the joint fundraising agreements signed by both Clinton and Sanders campaigns in 2015.<br /> <br /> But a senior Democrat with knowledge of the situation tells CNN that Brazile was referring to a separate agreement with the DNC that gave the campaign considerable control of the party.</b><br /> <br /> The agreement outlined that Clinton campaign personnel &quot;will be consulted and have joint authority over strategic decision over the staffing, budget, expenditures and general election related communications, data, technology, analytics and research. The DNC will provide HFA (Hillary for America) advance opportunity to review online or mass email, communications that features a particular Democratic primary candidate.&quot; </div> </div> </div>That's why this is an issue, because it turns out that while the DNC was publicly signing a joint fundraising agreement with Hillary and Bernie and acting as if it was a neutral party, it had also quietly signed a separate agreement that gave Hillary a highly questionable amount of power over the DNC itself, making it extremely difficult for the DNC to remain neutral during the Democratic Primary.<br /> <br /> While Brazile's story is very self-serving. Let's not forget she was trying to pass debate question to the Clinton campaign and she must have had knowledge that the DNC had already signed this agreement with Hillary even before Shultz stepped down. Still that doesn't change the fact that the DNC did sign onto this pretty questionable agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-04-2017, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T09:32:58-07:00","id":1155752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1155233-donna-brazill-comes-clean-on-dnc-corruption?p=1155717#post1155717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am under the impression that Donna's story is <i>not</i> about joint fundraising agreements, but rather is about a completely separate and highly questionable agreement that the DNC signed with Clinton which gave Clinton an unusual amount of control over the DNC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which still comes back to the join fundraising agreements giving Clinton's campaign the power to do so. Basically, Clinton got to use the DNC like an incumbent president (aka how Obama and her husband both did in their second runs), because the DNC wasn't setup to stay neutral if one candidate was ready to play JFA ball, and the other didn't (and to a certain extent, why should it?).<br /> <br /> Hell, a contributing factor in all this was how Obama used the DNC in 2012 and left them broke... because the DNC was setup to cede a lot of power to a single candidate when that's the case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's why this is an issue,... </div> </div> </div>No, it explains why this - at worst - <b>was</b> an issue. Clinton and Sanders aren't running for president. Everyone involved is out (for now, plenty of the operatives will be back for whoever runs in 2020, but their job is to play the system for their campaign). The DNC is already instituting rules changes.<br /> <br /> There's nothing actually new here (again, this has all known months ago to anyone paying attention, even if we didn't have the texts of various internal memos), and it's doing nothing but distracting the left from being unified in opposition to the likes of Roy Moore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T10:58:55-07:00","id":1155792,"title":"","content":"I have a hard time giving people like Hilliary Clinton a break. She's gotten fairly lucky that people naturally contrast her with Donald Trump these days, but we shouldn't really forget that she's one of the living examples of why people felt disenfranchised enough to vote for someone like our current president.<br /> <br /> I am a little worried about a unified left for the same reason that I didn't like a unified right. Parties unified against each-other is a really great way to keep actual progress from being made across the board.<br /> <br /> Don't get me wrong, though, this administration needs some serious checks in place. It's just sad that we have to keep building on the foundations for the political cold war the tea party started.<br /> <br /> Remember when our biggest issue with politics was that people who got in would sell out some of their values to accomplish some of the other things they wanted done? I miss complaining about those things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:23:34-07:00","id":1155855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sparketh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1155233-donna-brazill-comes-clean-on-dnc-corruption?p=1155792#post1155792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a hard time giving people like Hilliary Clinton a break.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does it really matter? None of this is about giving her a break or not. It's about the public generally not being well informed on internal RNC and DNC politics, and finding out about them via stuff like people writing books after the fact that are purposefully being sold as sensational to get sold even if they're not really revealing anything unique.<br /> <br /> Her career as an elected official is over. However anyone feels about HRC is irrelevant to what to do in the future, and the fact that mentioning her gets any discussion of US politics away from actual issues speaks far more about the rest of us than it does her.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am a little worried about a unified left for the same reason that I didn't like a unified right. Parties unified against each-other is a really great way to keep actual progress from being made across the board. </div> </div> </div>Sure. But progress isn't really on the table right now. We're in a time when we actually need to rally against politicians that actively want America to be a Christian Theocratic state, and the Republicans are actively supporting his campaign because he'll vote for their tax plan.<br /> <br /> It seems kind of silly to point at Clinton as a reason people feel disenfranchised, when Trump is more likely president from Republican voter suppression laws letting him have the edge in all those really close states actually resulting in disenfranchisement.<br /> <br /> If the US right can't get unified against things that shouldn't be partisan issues along with the left, we're not in a place to let the left get broken apart to stop the people threatening all these things.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}